api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC109", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC111", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC113", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC115", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC117", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC119", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC121", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC123", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC125", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC127", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC129", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC131", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC133", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC135", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC137", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC139", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC141", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC143", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC145", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC147", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC149", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC151", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/PRC153", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/VIC010", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/VIC020", "https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/VIC030"], "references": [], "sent": "2026-08-28T09:17:00-04:00", "effective": "2026-08-28T09:17:00-04:00", "onset": "2026-08-28T09:17:00-04:00", "expires": "2026-08-29T16:00:00-04:00", "ends": null, "status": "Actual", "messageType": "Alert", "category": "Met", "severity": "Unknown", "certainty": "Possible", "urgency": "Future", "event": "Hydrologic Outlook", "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov", "senderName": "NWS San Juan PR", "headline": "Hydrologic Outlook issued August 28 at 9:17AM AST by NWS San Juan PR", "description": "ESFSJU\n\nThe National Hurricane Center is issuing advisories on Tropical Storm\nDolly, located nearly 1200 miles southeast of the local islands. The\nofficial forecast calls for Dolly to degenerate into a tropical wave\nbefore reaching the area on Sunday and Monday.\n\nSince the system is expected to find a hostile environment, a\nwidespread and long-lasting rainfall event is not anticipated.\nInstead, squally weather will bring periods of moderate to locally\nheavy rainfall, beginning late Sunday and stretching into Monday. In\ngeneral, we are anticipating rainfall accumulations of 1 to 3 inches,\nwhich will be beneficial for any areas receiving the rain. Lingering\nmoisture from the remnants of Dolly could contribute to additional\nshowers developing on Tuesday. The risk of flooding is low to locally\nmedium. Areas with the drainage system clogged by death vegetation\ndebris or urbanized areas with poor drainage could experience\nlocalized flooding.\n\nAny rainfall will be welcome, and could bring a temporary relieve to\nthe ongoing severe to extreme drought plaguing Puerto Rico and the\nVirgin Islands. However, the rain should not be enough to end the\ndrought.\n\nAt this time, the confidence in the forecast is medium, and the users\nare advised to monitor the forecast in case changes are introduced.\nIf that the case, this product will be update accordingly.", "instruction": null, "response": "Monitor", "note": null, "parameters": {"AWIPSidentifier": ["ESFSJU"], "WMOidentifier": ["FGCA72 TJSJ 281317"], "NWSheadline": ["Beneficial rains from the remnants of Tropical Storm Dolly are expected to reach Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands on Sunday and Monday"], "BLOCKCHANNEL": ["EAS", "NWEM", "CMAS"]}, "scope": "Public", "code": "IPAWSv1.0", "language": "en-US", "web": "http://www.weather.gov", "eventCode": {"SAME": ["NWS"], "NationalWeatherService": ["ESF"]}}}], "title": "Current watches, warnings, and advisories for Puerto Rico", "updated": "2026-08-29T05:01:00+00:00"}